Package: illume
Type: Package
Title: Exploration and Frequentist Inference in One Toolkit
Version: 0.0.6.9000
Authors@R: person(given = "Craig", family = "Hutton",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"),
                  email = "craig.hutton@gmail.com")
Description: A frequentist regression workflow built around inference rather
    than prediction. One engine fits gaussian, binomial, Poisson, negative
    binomial and multinomial models by approximate maximum likelihood using the
    Laplace approximation via 'RTMB', with 'lme4'-style formulas supporting
    crossed and nested random intercepts and slopes, penalised smooth terms via
    'mgcv', and AR(1) temporal correlation. Because one engine fits them all,
    every model shares a single object, a single set of methods, and a single
    diagnostic system that reports whether each assumption is consistent with
    the data, with a stated reason and suggested remedy when it is not. The
    multinomial family fits mixed models for nominal categorical outcomes, for
    which no frequentist implementation was previously available. Methods of
    Kristensen, Nielsen, Berg, Skaug and Bell (2016)
    <doi:10.18637/jss.v070.i05> and Halekoh and Hojsgaard (2014)
    <doi:10.18637/jss.v059.i09>.
